    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Full suite is green (38 tests, 0 failures) with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `contactPreference` as a read-time derived field on the owner response: `EMAIL` when the owner has a non-blank email, otherwise `PHONE`.\n\nThe response DTO is generated from the OpenAPI spec and populated by MapStruct, so the change mirrors the existing derived-field pattern (`locality`, `membershipLevel`):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field, serialized on both `GET` and `POST /api/owners`).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/ContactPreference.java`** (new) \u2014 helper deriving the value from the owner's email, kept out of `OwnerMapper` so MapStruct doesn't treat a `String`-returning method as an implicit mapping (same convention as `Locality`/`Membership`).\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired `contactPreference` via an `expression` `@Mapping`.\n\nBoth new `Cp27Tests` (`PHONE` when no email, `EMAIL` when present) pass, and no existing tests regressed.",
